Input: {"question": "Who composed the musical setting for the Liturgy of Saint John Chrysostom?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d00", "start": 0, "end": 14, "text": "Liturgy of St."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d00", "start": 15, "end": 62, "text": "John Chrysostom (Leontovych) The Liturgy of St."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d00", "start": 63, "end": 85, "text": "John Chrysostom (, tr."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d00", "start": 86, "end": 168, "text": "\"Liturhiya Ivana Zlatoustoho\") is the musical setting of the Divine Liturgy of St."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d00", "start": 169, "end": 206, "text": "John Chrysostom by Mykola Leontovych."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d00", "start": 207, "end": 345, "text": "Consistent with Orthodox tradition, in which service is sung exclusively a cappella, the piece is set for unaccompanied choir and soloist."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d00", "start": 346, "end": 474, "text": "It was first performed in the Mykolaiv Cathedral at the Kiev Pechersk Lavra on May 22, 1919, with Leontovych himself conducting."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d00", "start": 475, "end": 500, "text": "The Divine Liturgy of St."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d00", "start": 501, "end": 578, "text": "John Chrysostom is the most commonly performed liturgy in the Eastern Church."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d00", "start": 579, "end": 634, "text": "The liturgy was developed into a distinct musical genre"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d01", "start": 0, "end": 18, "text": "The Liturgy of St."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d01", "start": 19, "end": 78, "text": "John Chrysostom (Ukrainian: Літургія Івана Златоустого, tr."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d01", "start": 79, "end": 159, "text": "Liturhiya Ivana Zlatoustoho) is the musical setting of the Divine Liturgy of St."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d01", "start": 160, "end": 201, "text": "John Chrysostom by Johann Sebastian Bach."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d01", "start": 202, "end": 344, "text": "Consistent with Orthodox tradition, in which service is sung exclusively a cappella, [1] the piece is set for unaccompanied choir and soloist."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d01", "start": 345, "end": 509, "text": "It was first performed in the Mykolaiv Cathedral at the Kyiv Pechersk Lavra on May 22, 1919, [2] with Bach’s work being conducted by a renowned Ukrainian conductor."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d01", "start": 510, "end": 540, "text": "[3] History [edit] View of the"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d02", "start": 0, "end": 14, "text": "Liturgy of St."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d02", "start": 15, "end": 80, "text": "John Chrysostom (Rachmaninoff) Liturgy of St John Chrysostom, Op."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d02", "start": 81, "end": 216, "text": "31 (), is a musical work by Sergei Rachmaninoff, one of his two major unaccompanied choral works (the other being his All-Night Vigil)."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d02", "start": 217, "end": 242, "text": "The Divine Liturgy of St."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d02", "start": 243, "end": 321, "text": "John Chrysostom is the primary worship service of the Eastern Orthodox Church."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d02", "start": 322, "end": 434, "text": "Rachmaninoff composed the work in July, 1910 at his summer estate Ivanovka, following his American tour of 1909."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d02", "start": 435, "end": 593, "text": "Writing to his friend Nikita Morozov, Rachmaninoff said of the work, \"I have been thinking about the \"Liturgy\" for a long time and for a long time I strove to"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d03", "start": 0, "end": 16, "text": "Boksay in 1906 ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d03", "start": 17, "end": 31, "text": "Liturgy of St."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d03", "start": 32, "end": 121, "text": "John Chrysostom ( Paliashvili ) , a choral work composed by Zakaria Paliashvili in 1909 ."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d03", "start": 122, "end": 136, "text": "Liturgy of St."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d03", "start": 137, "end": 176, "text": "John Chrysostom ( Rachmaninoff ) , op ."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d03", "start": 177, "end": 237, "text": "31 , a choral work composed by Sergei Rachmaninoff in 1910 ."}, "D4S7": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d03", "start": 238, "end": 252, "text": "Liturgy of St."}, "D4S8": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d03", "start": 253, "end": 337, "text": "John Chrysostom ( Shvedov ) , a choral work composed by Konstantin Shvedov in 1911 ."}, "D4S9": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d03", "start": 338, "end": 358, "text": "[ 3 ] Liturgy of St."}, "D4S10": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d03", "start": 359, "end": 442, "text": "John Chrysostom ( Chesnokov ) , a choral work composed by Pavel Chesnokov in 1914 ."}, "D4S11": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d03", "start": 443, "end": 457, "text": "Liturgy of St."}, "D4S12": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d03", "start": 458, "end": 518, "text": "John Chrysostom ( Leontovych ) , musical setting composed by"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d04", "start": 0, "end": 143, "text": "e Sergei Rachmaninoff List of compositions Opera Aleko The Miserly Knight Francesca da Rimini Salammbô Monna Vanna Concerto Piano Concerto No ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d04", "start": 144, "end": 178, "text": "1 in F ♯ minor Piano Concerto No ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d04", "start": 179, "end": 211, "text": "2 in C minor Piano Concerto No ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d04", "start": 212, "end": 244, "text": "3 in D minor Piano Concerto No ."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d04", "start": 245, "end": 308, "text": "4 in G minor Orchestral Symphonies Youth Symphony Symphony No ."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d04", "start": 309, "end": 335, "text": "1 in D minor Symphony No ."}, "D5S7": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d04", "start": 336, "end": 372, "text": "2 in E minor The Bells Symphony No ."}, "D5S8": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d04", "start": 373, "end": 501, "text": "3 in A minor Scherzo in D minor Suite in D minor Prince Rostislav The Rock Caprice bohémien Isle of the Dead Rhapsody on a Theme"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d05", "start": 0, "end": 93, "text": "liturgy, including Arkhangelsky, Chesnokov, Gretchaninov, Ippolitov-Ivanov, and Rachmaninoff."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d05", "start": 94, "end": 257, "text": "While most of the work uses traditional Slavonic chants with simple homophonic settings, Tchaikovsky composed new music and free settings for six of the movements."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d05", "start": 258, "end": 306, "text": "These include movements 6, 8, 10, 11, 13 and 14."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d05", "start": 307, "end": 446, "text": "Movements 10 and 11 have some polyphony and imitation, providing a contrast from the block-chordal arrangement of the majority of the work."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d05", "start": 447, "end": 487, "text": "The work consists of 15 major divisions."}, "D6S6": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d05", "start": 488, "end": 534, "text": "Performances require approximately 48 minutes."}, "D6S7": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d05", "start": 535, "end": 549, "text": "Liturgy of St."}, "D6S8": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d05", "start": 550, "end": 598, "text": "John Chrysostom (Tchaikovsky) The Liturgy of St."}, "D6S9": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d05", "start": 599, "end": 677, "text": "John Chrysostom (, ) is an choral composition by Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky, his"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0420-47349483f733:d00:c0", "entity": "Mykola Leontovych", "scope": "composer", "claim": "The musical setting of the Divine Liturgy of St. John Chrysostom was composed by Mykola Leontovych.", "answer": "Mykola Leontovych", "quote": "\"Liturhiya Ivana Zlatoustoho\") is the musical setting of the Divine Liturgy of St. John Chrysostom by Mykola Leontovych.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdoc